# Licences

COMPUTEX.md is dual-licensed by kind of material.

## Content — CC BY 4.0

Everything under `knowledge/` (article text, fact tables, curation), plus the
generated data under `public/api/`, is licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International** licence.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may copy, redistribute, remix and build on it, including commercially, as long
as you give attribution. Attribution format:

    COMPUTEX.md, "{page title}", {URL}, retrieved {date}.
    Independent open-data project; not affiliated with COMPUTEX or TAITRA.

**Why CC BY rather than CC BY-SA.** The upstream project Taiwan.md uses CC BY-SA 4.0.
We deliberately chose the more permissive CC BY because the entire point of this
archive is to be quoted — by search engines, by language models, by trade press, by
the exhibitors themselves. ShareAlike puts a condition on commercial republication
that would deter exactly the reuse we want. This is possible because COMPUTEX.md
writes its own content and does not carry over any CC BY-SA material from upstream;
see the note below.

